# Build context for ./Containerfile. It COPYs build/deploy/ and nothing else, so everything
# else is dead weight -- and not a small amount of it: podman and docker both tar the whole
# context before the first instruction runs, and .zig-cache alone reaches tens of GB.
#
# Named .dockerignore rather than .containerignore because podman reads this one too (it
# prefers .containerignore and falls back here), while docker only reads this one.
#
# The four-line form is deliberate. `*` followed by `!build/deploy` is the obvious spelling
# and is unreliable: excluding a parent directory can stop the walk before the negation is
# ever considered. Excluding and re-including one level at a time is the portable idiom.
/*
!/build
/build/*
!/build/deploy
